[4/200] Running: Describe how attention mechanism improves translation models...

🧠 LLM Response:


In sequence-to-sequence models, an attention mechanism allows the decoder to focus on different parts of the input sequence at each step. This allows the model to selectively focus on relevant information in the source sequence, improving the accuracy of the translation. By weighting the input sequence according to the current decoder state, the model can selectively attend to different parts of the source sequence, allowing it to translate complex sentences more accurately. This is particularly useful in languages where word order is different from English, as it allows the model to focus on the correct parts of the input sequence even if they are in a different order. Overall, the attention mechanism improves translation models by allowing them to focus on the most relevant parts of the input sequence at each step, resulting in more accurate translations.
