    we extract paragraphs about the selected entities to represent
    knowledge hallucinations.

-   [Quanto](https://github.com/huggingface/quanto) (see
    [`prompts.json`](https://github.com/lauragift21/lm_humans_dialogue/blob/main/ hallucinations_prompts/prompts.json)),
    which extracts git-informed conversational prompts from several
    million of the most popular open-source projects on Github.

-   Based on stakeholder feedback, we manually created five use cases to
    represent conversational scenarios between teachers, students, and the
    AI language model, and our language model instructed the students on
    various technical subjects. We used this process to arrive at 48
    prompts for testing PRH.

It is essential to define the prompting strategy when prompting the
model while simultaneously considering the types of hallucinations that
are tested against. For example, under prompting the KG, use one of the
following strategies to evaluate knowledge hallucinations from the
Wikipedia corpus:

-   **direct retrieval prompt**: instruct the model to directly
    retrieve information from the provided Wikipedia abstract.

-   **appropriated question-answering prompt**: prompt the conversational
    agent using a conversational opening or story, then follow up with
    an appropriate question that can be answered based on the provided
    context.

For PRH, the stripped prompt format was:

> As a teacher, I need to know the **topic of your most recent course**.

which would lead to a generated response that looks like:

> My latest course was on Neural Machine Translation and I taught it to 30 Master’s students over 14 weeks.

In Step 3, we explore various evaluation metrics for hallucinations. It
might be desirable to instrument the experimental pipeline to compute
multiple metrics, which will help to better distinguish specific types
of hallucination.

